# Site information architecture

## Main nav

Primary practice links only: **Works · About · CV**.

Do not add secondary surfaces (Studio / design-for-hire, Writing go-live, Maps, Blog mirrors, external profiles) to the main nav without an explicit request.

## Footer

Secondary and site-wide links live in the footer: Works, About, CV, Studio, plus external/professional links (email, Instagram, GitHub, LinkedIn, Concordia, etc.) as already wired.

- **Maps** (`/maps`) — staged / not live yet: routes build, but stay out of the footer and sitemap (`noindex`) until go-live (satellite + trees + resettled + railway 1931 + Natural Resources 1941; Mapbox needs `PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN`)
- **Research** (`/research`) — staged / not live yet: content library + detail routes build, but stay out of nav, footer, and sitemap (`noindex`) until go-live. Email capture: `research@adamsimms.xyz` → R2 inbox (see `docs/RESEARCH-INBOX.md`); promote/admin is phase 3.
- **Studio** (`/studio`) → footer, not main nav (publication / web work for others + hire CTA)
- **Newsletter** — quiet footer signup (`NewsletterSignup`) → Worker `art-adamsimms-xyz-newsletter` (D1 list). Needs `PUBLIC_NEWSLETTER_URL`. Do not put newsletter in main nav.
- Keep the footer quiet — short labels, no link farm

## CV

The CV is two columns. Left: Education, Teaching, Affiliations, Juries, Awards, Design + Technology. Right: Solo Exhibitions, Group Exhibitions, Public Art, Residencies + Workshops, Talks, Writing, Bibliography, Press. Instagram, LinkedIn, and GitHub live under **Elsewhere**: after Design + Technology in the first column on desktop, last on the page (after Press) on one-column / mobile. Email stays in the footer on screen and prints under the CV title. Teaching stays in the footer and the CV Teaching section.

Print: hide site header, footer, and cursor. Keep two columns. Show `hello@adamsimms.xyz`.

Punctuation on a CV line. A line is fields. The mark depends on what sits on either side.

- **Comma** stays inside one field. Place (`Montreal, Quebec, 2021`). A bibliographic cluster (`Riddle Fence, St. John’s, Issue 14` or `James D. Campbell, Ciel variable, Montreal, CV92`). A job title (`Artist-in-Residence, Studio Arts`). Bibliography lines always include the publication city. CV cities use English `Montreal` unless the city is inside a quoted legal or publication name.
- **Spaced en dash** (` – `) sits between fields. Title – venue – place. Degree – program. Role – person. Role – talk – venue. Work – credit – year.
- **Parentheses** wrap a subordinate label, not a peer field. Course code (`Digital Photography I (PHOT 331)`). Talk series (`Virtual Identity for Artists (Survival Tactics)`). Status or parent org (`(upcoming)`, `(Atlassian)`).
- **Unspaced en dash** (`2018–2019`) is a year range inside the date field. Hyphens stay in compound words (`Washed-up`).

The place/date cluster is one field, so it uses commas even though institution, city, and year are different facts. Do not put ` – ` inside that cluster. Do not use ` – ` between two names for the same thing. Do not use `•` or `/` on the CV. List markers are the hairline L.

## Writing

Long-form essays can live at `/writing/[slug]` before they appear in nav. Discoverability via CV (and later an index) is enough until the Writing SEO go-live checklist in `writing-seo.mdc` is done.

## Research

Working library of books, essays, places, concepts, etc. at `/research` and `/research/[slug]`. See `research-content.mdc`. Keep off main nav and footer until explicitly asked to un-hide.

## Homepage brand

On the homepage, the site title always shows the full name **Adam Simms** — never the condensed **AS** treatment used elsewhere when space is tight.
